  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When someone runs this against fedora, they still get all the user managed triples:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "`curl -H \"prefer:return=representation; omit=\\\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#PreferMinimalContainer"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#PreferMinimalContainer\\",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"\" ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://localhost:8080/fcrepo510/rest/BasicContainer/BasicContainer1"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://localhost:8080/fcrepo510/rest/BasicContainer/BasicContainer1",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin`",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "With the `PreferMinimalContainer` in the `omit` list, one would expect that the user managed triples would be excluded.   Fedora is only paying attention to `PreferMinimalContainer` when it is in the `include` list.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
