  "description": "<p>When someone runs this against fedora, they still get all the user managed triples:</p>\n\n<p>`curl -H \"prefer:return=representation; omit=\\\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#PreferMinimalContainer\\\"\" <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fcrepo510/rest/BasicContainer/BasicContainer1\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fcrepo510/rest/BasicContainer/BasicContainer1</a> -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin`</p>\n\n<p>With the `PreferMinimalContainer` in the `omit` list, one would expect that the user managed triples would be excluded.   Fedora is only paying attention to `PreferMinimalContainer` when it is in the `include` list.</p>",
